rrect answer is \"All real numbers.\"" 13194139545672 17592186576411 true] [17592186234082 1074 "Let's recall the graph of $y={log}_{9}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/40/40664f83ba162a93ed06970798d37798db90b85c21d44a9ed20f338df4e1b4e1.png)\n\nThe domain of $y={log}_{9}⁡x$ is $x\\in (0,\\infty )$ and the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"All real numbers.\"" 13194139545672 17592186576411 false] [17592186234108 1071 "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{\\cos }^{2}⁡(-\\pi +\\frac{\\pi k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{n}].\n$$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 true] [17592186234108 1071 "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{cos}^{2}⁡(-\\pi +\\frac{\\pi k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{n}].\n$$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 false] [17592186234108 1074 "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=-\\pi .$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{\\pi }{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{n}=\\frac{b-(-\\pi )}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=0.\n$$\n\nConsequently, ${x}_{k}=-\\pi +\\frac{\\pi k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})={\\cos }^{2}⁡{x}_{k}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}{\\cos }^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\lim_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{\\cos }^{2}⁡(-\\pi +\\frac{\\pi k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(x)={\\cos }^{2}⁡x$ and $b=0.$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 true] [17592186234108 1074 "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f