ps:\n\n* Start with the graph of $y=\\sin ⁡x.$\n\n* Then, shift it by $1$ units **up**.\n\nThe resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/db/dbe1701a42a160e982bff96b1085727080c39b87ca2c99886e3e153e2f5964cc.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the maximum value is $y=2.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe know that $y=\\sin ⁡x$ has a maximum value of $1.$ \n\n$$\n\\sin ⁡x\\le 1\n$$\n\nAdding $1$ to both sides of the above inequality gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin ⁡x+1\\le 1+1 \\\\ \\sin ⁡x+1\\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the maximum value of $\\sin ⁡x+1$ is $A=2.$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 true] [17592186235453 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n* Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n* Then, shift it by $1$ units **up**.\n\nThe resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/db/dbe1701a42a160e982bff96b1085727080c39b87ca2c99886e3e153e2f5964cc.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the maximum value is $y=2.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe know that $y=sin⁡x$ has a maximum value of $1.$ \n\n$$\nsin⁡x\\le 1\n$$\n\nAdding $1$ to both sides of the above inequality gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sin⁡x+1\\le 1+1 \\\\ sin⁡x+1\\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the maximum value of $sin⁡x+1$ is $A=2.$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 false] [17592186235454 1071 "![](images/6e/6e1d2c8fef007596dc6fd9b6ef0813fafeb7014490ff35d993f276a2a96ccb13.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\nIf the graph above is generated by the function $y=\\sin ⁡(Bx),$ then $B=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." 13194139545672 17592186576411 true] [17592186235454 1071 "![](images/6e/6e1d2c8fef007596dc6fd9b6ef0813fafeb7014490ff35d993f276a2a96c