rix and $\\det (B)=-75.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{2}$ and ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{6}.$ What is the value of $\\det (C)?$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 true] [17592186265972 1071 "Suppose $B$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(B)=-75.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{2}$ and ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{6}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 false] [17592186265972 1074 "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{6}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{2}$ involves multiplying a row by $\\frac{4}{5},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $\\frac{4}{5}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $\\frac{4}{5}$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det (C) & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-\\det (B)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\det (B) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-75) \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 true] [17592186265972 1074 "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{6}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{2}$ involves multiplying a row by $\\frac{4}{5},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $\\frac{4}{5}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $\\frac{4}{5}$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-det(B)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}det(B) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-75) \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 false] [17592186265985 1071 "Given that $\\det (A)=\\det (B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 true] [17592186265985 1071 "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 false] [17592186265985 1074 "Since $\\det (A)=\\det (B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det (A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\det (B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 true] [17592186265985 1074 "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$" 131941395