 Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 true] [17592186275403 1074 "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{x}{5} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 false] [17592186275408 1071 "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{{\\cos }^{2}⁡x}$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 true] [17592186275408 1071 "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139545672 17592186576411 false] [17592186275408 1074 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{y}{{\\cos }^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{{\\cos }^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{\\cos }^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\f